  "kind": "windows-realesrgan-worker-path-fix",
  "status": "passed",
  "task": "team task-11",
  "root_cause": "Rust Path::canonicalize returns an extended-length '\\\\?\\C:\\...' path on Windows. The worker compared it byte-wise against the plain input path, so every normal absolute path was rejected; passing the verbatim form instead made ncnn fail (_wfopen cannot open '\\\\?\\' paths, exit 0xc0000409). A second Windows-only discrepancy surfaced in the real exchange: the official Windows ncnn build always writes RGBA PNGs while the frozen v2 contract requires exactly one 8-bit RGB candidate (the macOS build writes RGB).",
  "fix": [
    "trusted_user_path() keeps the previous validation (absolute, not a symlink, canonicalizable, already normalized, file/directory kind) and on Windows strips the '\\\\?\\C:\\' / '\\\\?\\UNC\\' verbatim prefix; input and canonical paths are compared case-insensitively with '/' folded to '\\'.",
    "--ncnn-binary, model_path, output_dir and the source input path all use trusted_user_path(); the ncnn -i/-o/-m arguments are plain absolute paths without the verbatim prefix.",
    "normalize_ncnn_png() leaves existing 8-bit RGB output byte-identical (macOS behavior) and rewrites opaque 8-bit RGBA output (the Windows ncnn build) as an 8-bit RGB PNG; non-opaque alpha is rejected instead of dropped.",
    "ncnn binary, model weight and source image SHA-256/size verification logic is unchanged."
  ],
